# build.cfg.example -- template for build.cfg, which tells the build where
# the things lie that are not part of the repository.
#
# Copy it to build.cfg in the repository root and fill in what differs.
# build.cfg holds your own paths and never goes into the repository
# (.gitignore).  You need it only if a file is not at its default place:
# a folder ambermoon_gamedata/ next to the repository.  An environment
# variable of the same name wins over this file.
#
# One KEY=PATH per line (AMBER_FALCON: KEY=ADDRESS); # starts a comment; ~ is your home directory; a
# relative path is relative to this file.  Every build shows at the start,
# under "Sources and switches", what it took from where; the same overview:
# python3 tools/paths.py

# The game files of one version (Thalion's 1.01, 1.07, 1.20, Pyrdacor's
# 1.2x): the directory *above* Amberfiles/, the Amberfiles folder itself,
# a zip as downloaded, or the disk images (a folder with the ADF, DMS or
# IPF files, or one of them; DMS needs xdms).  Not set and the default
# missing: the build takes the one set of game files it finds in
# ambermoon_gamedata/ (tools/game_files.py).  For one build, name them on the
# command line instead: sh tools/build_all.sh ambermoone.zip
# Default: ambermoon_gamedata/ambermoon_german_1.20_extracted
#AMBER_DATEN=~/ambermoon_gamedata/ambermoon_german_1.20_extracted
#AMBER_DATEN=~/Downloads/ambermoone.zip

# Thalion's released source, the folder that holds GAME_OFF.S
# (github.com/jhorneman/ambermoon, folder src).  Not set and the default
# missing: the build takes a clone or zip of it from ambermoon_gamedata/,
# else it fetches the tested commit from GitHub (tools/fetch_source.py).
# Default: ambermoon_gamedata/ambermoon-main-asm/src
#AMBER_URCODE=~/ambermoon_gamedata/ambermoon-main-asm/src

# NO: the build never fetches anything from the network (Thalion's source,
# vasm and vlink).
#AMBER_DOWNLOAD=NO

# Optional: Big Alec's YM music, big_alec/ambermon.snd from the SNDH
# archive, downloaded by hand from https://sndh.atari.org/?ID=5364.
# Without it the YM stays silent.
# Default: ambermoon_gamedata/ambermon.snd
#AMBER_YMSNDH=~/ambermoon_gamedata/ambermon.snd

# Optional: a TOS image, only for the emulator Hatari (tools/hatari/).
# Default: ambermoon_gamedata/TOS404.IMG
#AMBER_TOS=~/ambermoon_gamedata/TOS404.IMG

# Optional: an m68k objdump.  Without it the build searches PATH and the
# VS Code extension atari-st-dev.
#AMBER_OBJDUMP=/opt/cross-mint/bin/m68k-atari-mintelf-objdump

# Optional: the network address of your test Falcon running uIPtool, for
# python3 tools/testpaket.py falcon.  An address, not a path.
#AMBER_FALCON=192.168.0.10
